# Docs → Cursor rules map

Do **not** duplicate rule text into `docs/`. Load the right source:

## Always applied (this folder)
| Rule | Covers |
|---|---|
| `conventions.mdc` | Coding boundaries, ledger, RLS, naming, secrets |
| `decisions.mdc` | MVP scope deltas (no Fayda/USSD, CoA, eligibility, seed) |

## Request when relevant
| Rule | When |
|---|---|
| `git-workflow.mdc` | Branches, commits, PRs, merge order, migration conflicts |
| `task-plan.mdc` | Picking next work, ownership, task dependencies |

## Stay in `docs/` only (read on demand — do not invent from memory)
| File | Use for |
|---|---|
| `docs/TASKS.md` | Master build order, verify steps |
| `docs/TEAM_ASSIGNMENTS.md` | Same plan by person / vertical |
| `docs/TEAM_STATUS.md` | Who is blocked / in progress right now |
| `docs/SACCO_PROPOSAL.md` | Background SDS only — **MVP truth is `decisions.mdc`** |
| `docs/README.md` | Index of the docs folder |
